Videos Of Moroccan Migrants Go Viral On X
Videos of large numbers of migrants appearing to cross the Spanish border into Ceuta went widely viral on social media Thursday, frequently circulated by right-wing commentators who are critical of immigration. Billionaire Elon Musk said on Thursday afternoon the migration surge is “absolutely an invasion,” among several posts he made on the situation in Ceuta. He later shared a video purportedly showing the migrant surge while adding the comment “Looks like World War Z!” after posting, “Spain’s entire budget will be destroyed by illegal migrants.” A video posted to X by Santiago Abascal, leader of Spain’s far-right Vox party, also called the influx of migrants an “invasion” and accused “Sánchez's corrupt government” of “desperately calling in more hitmen to stay in power.” Abascal’s video garnered more than 2.2 million views as of Thursday afternoon. Abascal posted another video Thursday morning, garnering 2.6 million views, accusing Sánchez of being a “traitor, a corrupt man, and an indecent person,” calling for his ouster.
