Mr Kissi was eventually picked up by the Moroccan navy and returned to Saidia, he continued.
The other man who was killed has been named as Abdelali Merchouer.
The fourth man, named as Smail Snabe, was arrested by the Algerian coastguard and is understood to have appeared before an Algerian prosecutor on Wednesday.
A Moroccan government spokesman refused to comment describing the incident as ""a matter for the judiciary"".
Algeria has not commented either.
Algeria and Morocco’s dispute centres on Western Sahara, with the 1,242-mile border which the countries share a huge bone of contention.
