71 The oldest written documentation that the authors have found is Saugnier, F. and Brisson, P. (1792) Voyages to the Coast of Africa by Mess. Saugnier and Brisson, Containing an Account of their Shipwreck on Board Different Vessels, and Subsequent Slavery, and Interesting Details of the Manners of the Arabs of the Desert. London: G.G.J. and J. Robinson. p. 35. Shipwrecked Mr Saugnier, ‘abducted’ at Boujdour (modern day Western Sahara) by ‘wandering Arabs’, marvels at the Saharawis’ ecologically-aware practices, such as their insistence on only using dead wood for kindling and never any live shrubs.
